From b1456805884084231b84f7cbf9989a8ee851a875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 06:39:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bifrost: re-vendor wire.rs from canonical to fix protocol
 drift

scripts/check-proto-drift.sh failed because the vendored guest
wire.rs SHA pin no longer matched canonical host/bifrost-wire/src/
lib.rs.  Re-vendoring the body and bumping CANONICAL_SHA256 closes
the drift; the canonical changes were comment-only (protocol-arc
docstring + lquantize doc), but the SHA pin is the ABI gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/bifrost/wire.rs | 149 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 97 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

